function Intro(){return <section className="hero"><div className="wrap"><div className="eyebrow">INTERACTIVE WORKSHOP</div><h1>Stop Starting.<br/><em>Start Finishing.</em></h1><p>When everything is started at once, finishing becomes harder. Learn to see where work gets stuck, make better decisions when plans change, and improve how work gets done—at home, on a team, or across an organization.</p><div className="home-entry-actions"><a className="btn home-start-cta" href="#choose-simulation">Start Learning <ArrowRight size={18}/></a><a className="home-entry-secondary" href="#flow-assessment">Explore the Flow Assessment <ArrowRight size={15}/></a></div><p className="home-entry-hint">No account needed for the one-screen experiences. Choose your starting point below.</p></div></section>}
function LearningJourney(){return <section className="wrap home-learning-journey" aria-labelledby="learning-journey-title"><div className="eyebrow dark">START SIMPLE · GO FURTHER WHEN YOU'RE READY</div><h2 id="learning-journey-title">Experience. Understand. Improve.</h2><p className="home-learning-intro">You don't need to know Kanban to begin. Try one practical experience, learn what the results might mean, and explore a small improvement when it helps. Choose only what is useful to you.</p><div className="home-learning-grid"><article className="home-learning-card"><span className="home-learning-number">01</span><div className="home-learning-symbol"><Play size={22}/></div><h3>Experience</h3><p>Try a simulation and see what happens when work piles up, priorities shift, or people help each other finish.</p><a href="#choose-simulation">Choose an experience <ArrowRight size={15}/></a></article><article className="home-learning-card"><span className="home-learning-number">02</span><div className="home-learning-symbol"><ChartColumnIncreasing size={23}/></div><h3>Understand</h3><p>Explore one metric at a time. Ask what the numbers reveal—and what you still need to ask the people doing the work.</p><a href="#data-and-story">Explore the data <ArrowRight size={15}/></a></article><article className="home-learning-card"><span className="home-learning-number">03</span><div className="home-learning-symbol"><Compass size={23}/></div><h3>Improve</h3><p>See which practices you already use, where work causes stress, and what small change could be worth testing.</p><a href="#flow-assessment">Explore the assessment <ArrowRight size={15}/></a></article></div><p className="home-learning-reassurance">No required order. No maturity score. No need to track every metric. Start with one useful idea.</p></section>}
function FoundationalDetails(){return <section className="wrap home-deeper-learning"><details className="home-deeper-disclosure"><summary><span><strong>Want to see how the foundational simulation works?</strong><small>Explore the three phases and the card rules before you play.</small></span><span className="home-deeper-toggle" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div className="home-deeper-inner"><HowDetails/></div></details></section>}
function VideoPreviewPlaceholder(){return <section className="wrap lab-video-section" aria-labelledby="lab-video-title"><div className="lab-video-copy"><div className="eyebrow dark">SEE LEARNING IN ACTION</div><h2 id="lab-video-title">Watch the Lab in Action</h2><p>See people work through the simulation, make decisions together, and discover what happens when they limit the work they start.</p><p className="lab-video-note">A short demonstration with real participants is planned. In the meantime, you can explore the simulations yourself.</p><a href="#choose-simulation" className="btn primary">Explore the simulations <ArrowRight size={16}/></a></div><div className="lab-video-frame" aria-label="Demonstration video coming soon"><div className="lab-video-play" aria-hidden="true"><Play size={29}/></div><strong>Real teams. Real decisions.</strong><span>Video demonstration coming soon</span></div></section>}
function WhyFlowWorks(){return <section className="flow-why" aria-labelledby="flow-why-heading"><div className="wrap"><div className="eyebrow dark">WHY THIS MATTERS</div><h2 id="flow-why-heading">You cannot improve what you cannot see.</h2><p className="flow-why-lede">Think about a day when you have ten things underway but nothing finished. Starting another task rarely fixes that. The same challenge shows up in families, classrooms, service teams, hospitals, factories, and entire companies.</p><div className="flow-why-example"><div className="flow-why-contrast"><div className="flow-why-mini"><span className="flow-why-mini-label">Busy isn't always progress</span><div className="flow-why-bars" aria-hidden="true"><span/><span/><span/><span/><span/></div><strong>Lots started. Little finished.</strong></div><div className="flow-why-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</div><div className="flow-why-mini focused"><span className="flow-why-mini-label">Focus makes progress visible</span><div className="flow-why-bars" aria-hidden="true"><span/><span/><span className="done"/><span className="done"/><span className="done"/></div><strong>Less at once. More room to finish.</strong></div></div><p>This is a teaching example, not a promise that limiting work always increases output. The simulation lets you test what actually happens.</p></div><div className="flow-why-benefits"><article><span className="flow-why-number">01</span><h3>See the work</h3><p>Make commitments, waiting, and obstacles visible so people can understand what's happening.</p></article><article><span className="flow-why-number">02</span><h3>Finish what matters</h3><p>Explore how limiting work in progress changes focus, handoffs, and teamwork.</p></article><article><span className="flow-why-number">03</span><h3>Learn from evidence</h3><p>Use measures as clues to understand the system—not as scores to judge people.</p></article></div><div className="flow-resilience" aria-labelledby="flow-resilience-title"><div className="eyebrow dark">WHEN THE PLAN CHANGES</div><h3 id="flow-resilience-title">Real life rarely follows a perfect plan.</h3><p>Someone gets sick. A customer changes priorities. A dependency delays progress. A new tool or AI system changes how work is done. The goal is not to follow one rigid process—it is to make what is happening visible, think critically, and adapt together.</p><div className="flow-resilience-grid"><article><b>Make the real workflow visible</b><span>A simple To-Do → In Progress → Done board can help you start. As work grows, show actual steps, such as development, review, testing, and approval, so waiting and bottlenecks do not stay hidden.</span></article><article><b>Ask better questions with data</b><span>Lead time, aging work, throughput, and blocked time help explain where work waits and why. No single number tells the whole story, and waiting is not always waste.</span></article><article><b>Improve before automating</b><span>New technology—including AI—may speed up parts of a process. First understand the work, its quality, and its constraints so automation does not simply accelerate existing problems.</span></article></div><p className="flow-resilience-close">Kanban Flow Lab helps you practice decisions under both predictable and unexpected conditions. Learn the basics with the foundational simulations, then explore changing demand, tradeoffs, and uncertainty in <a href="#flow-evolution">Flow Evolution Lab</a>.</p></div><div className="flow-why-scope"><h3>One idea. Every scale.</h3><div className="flow-why-scope-grid"><div><b>Personal</b><span>Organize chores, schoolwork, or personal goals without juggling everything at once.</span></div><div><b>Team</b><span>Coordinate priorities, make blockers visible, and help each other finish work.</span></div><div><b>Organization</b><span>See how handoffs, dependencies, and competing priorities affect delivery across groups.</span></div></div></div><div className="flow-why-close"><div><h3>You don't need to know Kanban to begin.</h3><p>Try a simulation, see the results, and decide what you would change. These experiences are built for discovery, not for grading people.</p></div><a className="btn primary" href="#choose-simulation">Choose a simulation <ArrowRight size={16}/></a></div></div></section>}
function ChooseSimulation(){return <section className="wrap choose-simulation" id="choose-simulation" aria-label="Choose your simulation"><div className="eyebrow dark">THREE WAYS TO EXPERIENCE FLOW</div><h2>Choose your simulation experience</h2><p className="muted">Choose the experience that fits you. You can start on your own, work through decisions together, or challenge a team that already uses Kanban.</p><div className="home-audience-guidance" aria-label="Find your starting point"><div><strong>Learning on your own?</strong><span>Start with Facilitated Simulation in Automatic or Manual mode.</span></div><div><strong>Leading a group?</strong><span>Use Facilitated for one shared screen, or Collaborative for multiple devices.</span></div><div><strong>Already practicing Kanban?</strong><span>Try Flow Evolution Lab for changing demand and improvement experiments.</span></div></div><div className="choose-grid"><article className="choose-card"><div className="choose-icon"><Monitor size={25}/></div><h3>Facilitated Simulation</h3><p className="choose-subtitle">One screen. Shared decisions. Guided learning.</p><p>Ideal for classrooms and workshops. One person operates the board while participants explore flow, WIP limits, and team behaviors together. Also supports individual and automatic practice.</p><a className="btn primary" href="#facilitated">Explore Facilitated <ArrowRight size={16}/></a></article><article className="choose-card"><div className="choose-icon"><Users size={25}/></div><h3>Collaborative Simulation</h3><p className="choose-subtitle">Multiple devices. One board. Real teamwork.</p><p>Ideal for distributed teams and interactive workshops. Join one shared board as a player, or create a room as a facilitator and invite students to participate from their own computers.</p><a className="btn primary" href="https://kanban-multiplayer.vercel.app" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Explore Collaborative <ExternalLink size={16}/></a></article><article className="choose-card"><div className="choose-icon"><Compass size={25}/></div><h3>Flow Evolution Lab</h3><p className="choose-subtitle">Advanced teams. New scenarios. Better decisions.</p><p>For teams that already practice Kanban. Three ten-day experiments challenge them with changing demand, unexpected scenarios, tradeoffs, team-selected WIP limits, and guided reflections.</p><a className="btn primary" href="#flow-evolution">Explore Flow Evolution <ArrowRight size={16}/></a></article></div></section>}
const metricLesson = {inProgress:'wip', blocked:'blocked', completed:'throughput', rate:'throughput', short:'lead-time',long:'lead-time',mean:'lead-time',p75:'percentiles',p85:'percentiles',p95:'percentiles',oldest:'age'};
function MetricLearn({id,label='Understand this metric'}){return <a className="metric-lesson-link" href={`https://kanbanflowlab.com/#metric-${id}`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style={{display:'inline-flex',alignItems:'center',marginLeft:8,gap:4,fontSize:12,fontWeight:650,color:'#97631c',textDecoration:'underline',textUnderlineOffset:3}} aria-label={`${label} (opens in a new tab)`}>{label} ↗</a>}
function Results({history,total,phaseLength,lateWip,playerNames,players}){const [visible,setVisible]=useState(true);const one=reportPeriod(history,0,20),three=reportPeriod(history,20,total,true);const before=phaseLength===20?reportPeriod(history,20,30,true):null,after=phaseLength===20?reportPeriod(history,30,40):null;if(!one||!three)return null;const compare=[['Days','days'],['Backlog','backlog'],['In Progress','inProgress'],['Blocked','blocked'],['Completed','completed'],['Throughput / day','rate'],['Shortest lead time','short'],['Longest lead time','long'],['Average lead time','mean'],['75th percentile','p75'],['85th percentile','p85'],['95th percentile','p95'],['Oldest unfinished age','oldest']];const display=(v,key)=>['short','long','mean','p75','p85','p95','oldest'].includes(key)?formatDays(v):key==='rate'?v.toFixed(2):v;
const chartData=(p)=>p.cfd.map(r=>({day:r.day,Done:r.completed,Review:r.review,'Working on':r.working,'To-Do':r.backlog}));
const highest=Math.max(1,...one.daily.map(d=>d.count),...three.daily.map(d=>d.count));
const leadMax=Math.max(1,...one.leadTimes,...three.leadTimes);const frequency=(p)=>Array.from({length:leadMax},(_,i)=>({days:i+1,tasks:p.leadTimes.filter(v=>v===i+1).length}));
return <section className="results panel"><div className="section-row"><div><div className="eyebrow dark">COMPLETE</div><h2>Final performance report</h2></div><button className="btn small secondary" onClick={()=>setVisible(v=>!v)}>{visible?'Hide':'Show'} report</button></div>{visible&&<>{playerNames.some(x=>x.trim())&&<div className="name-setup"><b>Participants</b><p className="muted small-text">{playerNames.map((n,i)=>`P${i+1}: ${n.trim()||'Not named'}`).slice(0,players).join('  ·  ')}</p></div>}<p className="muted">New to a metric? Select its Learn link to open a short explanation in another tab without losing these results.</p><p className="muted">Phases 1+2 use the original 20-day board. Phase 3 starts fresh and runs for {phaseLength} days. Compare throughput per day when durations differ.</p><div className="table-scroller"><table><thead><tr><th>Metric</th><th>Phases 1+2</th><th>Phase 3</th></tr></thead><tbody>{compare.map(([label,key])=><tr key={key}><td>{label}{metricLesson[key]&&<MetricLearn id={metricLesson[key]} label="Learn"/>}</td><td>{display(one[key],key)}</td><td>{display(three[key],key)}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
<h3>Cumulative flow diagrams <MetricLearn id="cfd"/></h3><div className="legend"><span><i style={{background:'#31977b'}}/>Done</span><span><i style={{background:'#588fcc'}}/>Review</span><span><i style={{background:'#e7aa60'}}/>Working on</span><span><i style={{background:'#a8afb9'}}/>Backlog</span></div>{[{p:one,title:'Phases 1+2',name:'wip3'},{p:three,title:'Phase 3',name:'late'}].map(({p,title,name})=><div className="chart-card" key={title}><h4>{title} · {p.days} days</h4><div className="chart-container"><ResponsiveContainer width="100%" height={255}><AreaChart data={chartData(p)} margin={{top:12,right:16,bottom:4,left:-15}}><CartesianGrid strokeDasharray="3 3" stroke="#e9edf3"/><XAxis dataKey="day" tick={{fontSize:11}}/><YAxis domain={[0,30]} tick={{fontSize:11}}/><Tooltip/><Area type="linear" dataKey="Done" stackId="1" fill="#31977b" stroke="#31977b"/><Area type="linear" dataKey="Review" stackId="1" fill="#588fcc" stroke="#588fcc"/><Area type="linear" dataKey="Working on" stackId="1" fill="#e7aa60" stroke="#e7aa60"/><Area type="linear" dataKey="To-Do" stackId="1" fill="#a8afb9" stroke="#a8afb9"/>{p.days===20&&<ReferenceLine x={10} stroke="#29364a" strokeDasharray="5 4" label={{value:name==='wip3'?'WIP 3 + DSU':'WIP adjustment',position:'insideTopRight',fontSize:10}}/>}</AreaChart></ResponsiveContainer></div>{name==='late'&&<p className="chart-note">Fresh Day 0: 30 backlog tasks, none started. {phaseLength===20?`WIP ${lateWip} begins on Day 31.`:'WIP 3 throughout.'}</p>}</div>)}
<h3>Daily throughput <MetricLearn id="throughput"/></h3><p className="muted">Each dot is one day, including days with zero completions. Both charts use the same vertical scale.</p>{[{p:one,title:'Phases 1+2',color:'#588fcc'},{p:three,title:'Phase 3',color:'#31977b'}].map(({p,title,color})=><div className="chart-card" key={title}><div className="section-row tight"><h4>{title} · {p.completed} completed</h4><span className="muted small-text">{p.rate.toFixed(2)} / day</span></div><div className="chart-container"><ResponsiveContainer width="100%" height={235}><LineChart data={p.daily} margin={{top:15,right:22,bottom:4,left:-15}}><CartesianGrid strokeDasharray="3 3" stroke="#e9edf3"/><XAxis dataKey="day" interval={0} tick={{fontSize:10}}/><YAxis allowDecimals={false} domain={[0,Math.max(4,highest)]} tick={{fontSize:11}}/><Tooltip/><Line type="linear" dataKey="count" name="Completed" stroke={color} strokeWidth={2.5} dot={{r:4,fill:color}} activeDot={{r:6}}/>{p.days===20&&<ReferenceLine x={10.5} stroke="#39495e" strokeDasharray="4 4"/>}</LineChart></ResponsiveContainer></div></div>)}
{before&&after&&<><h3>Phase 3 WIP experiment</h3><div className="table-scroller"><table><thead><tr><th>Metric</th><th>Days 21–30 · WIP 3</th><th>Days 31–40 · WIP {lateWip}</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Completions in period</td><td>{before.completed}</td><td>{after.completed-before.completed}</td></tr><tr><td>Throughput / day</td><td>{before.rate.toFixed(2)}</td><td>{((after.completed-before.completed)/10).toFixed(2)}</td></tr><tr><td>End In Progress</td><td>{before.inProgress}</td><td>{after.inProgress}</td></tr><tr><td>End Blocked</td><td>{before.blocked}</td><td>{after.blocked}</td></tr><tr><td>End Backlog</td><td>{before.backlog}</td><td>{after.backlog}</td></tr></tbody></table></div></>}
<h3>Lead-time histograms <MetricLearn id="lead-time"/></h3><p className="muted">Both histograms use the same day buckets and count only completed tasks.</p>{[{p:one,title:'Phases 1+2',color:'#588fcc'},{p:three,title:'Phase 3',color:'#31977b'}].map(({p,title,color})=><div className="chart-card" key={title}><div className="section-row tight"><h4>{title}</h4><span className="muted small-text">{p.completed} completed</span></div><div className="chart-container"><ResponsiveContainer width="100%" height={250}><BarChart data={frequency(p)} margin={{top:15,right:20,bottom:12,left:-15}}><CartesianGrid strokeDasharray="3 3" stroke="#e9edf3"/><XAxis dataKey="days" tick={{fontSize:10}} label={{value:'Lead time (days)',position:'insideBottom',offset:-6,fontSize:11}}/><YAxis allowDecimals={false} tick={{fontSize:11}}/><Tooltip/><Bar dataKey="tasks" name="Tasks" fill={color} maxBarSize={45}/></BarChart></ResponsiveContainer></div><div className="mini-summary"><span>Shortest: <b>{formatDays(p.short)}</b></span><span>Average: <b>{formatDays(p.mean)}</b></span><span>Longest: <b>{formatDays(p.long)}</b></span></div></div>)}<p className="chart-note">Percentiles describe observed lead times for completed tasks, not validated forecasting confidence. Unfinished tasks are excluded from lead-time charts; the oldest unfinished age is reported separately. Automated players follow fixed work-selection rules, and DSU leaders are randomly assigned but do not independently affect automated results.</p></>}</section>}
function Simulator(){const [players,setPlayers]=useState(5),[deck,setDeck]=useState(shuffleDeck),[dsu,setDsu]=useState(()=>assignLeaders(5)),[mode,setMode]=useState('manual'),[records,setRecords]=useState(initialHistory),[gate,setGate]=useState('start'),[phaseLength,setPhaseLength]=useState(null),[duration,setDuration]=useState(10),[lateWip,setLateWip]=useState(3),[wipChoice,setWipChoice]=useState(3),[inspect,setInspect]=useState(0),[day,setDay]=useState(1),[tasks,setTasks]=useState(freshBoard),[player,setPlayer]=useState(1),[selected,setSelected]=useState(1),[played,setPlayed]=useState([]),[blackParts,setBlackParts]=useState({}),[dayEvents,setDayEvents]=useState([]),[resetDialog,setResetDialog]=useState(false),[resetFresh,setResetFresh]=useState(false),[dsuChecks,setDsuChecks]=useState([false,false,false]),[dsuNotes,setDsuNotes]=useState('');
const [playerNames,setPlayerNames]=useState(['','','','','']);
const [draggedTask,setDraggedTask]=useState(null),[dragOverColumn,setDragOverColumn]=useState(null),[recentAction,setRecentAction]=useState(null);
useEffect(()=>{if(!recentAction)return;const timeout=setTimeout(()=>setRecentAction(null),1100);return ()=>clearTimeout(timeout);},[recentAction]);
const playerLabel=p=>{const name=(playerNames[p-1]||'').trim();return name?`P${p} · ${name}`:`P${p}`;};
const renameLog=event=>event.replace(/\bPlayer (\d+)\b|\bP(\d+)\b/g,(match,long,short)=>playerLabel(Number(long||short)));
const handsOn=mode==='manual'||mode==='facilitated',isFacilitated=mode==='facilitated',dsuComplete=dsuChecks.every(Boolean);const total=20+(phaseLength||0),currentDay=mode==='auto'?inspect:day,board=mode==='auto'?(records.find(r=>r.day===inspect)?.tasks||records[records.length-1].tasks):tasks,live=tally(board),people=Array.from({length:players},(_,i)=>i+1),playingCard=drawCard(deck,day,players,player),options=validActions(tasks,player,day,deck,players,lateWip,blackParts[player]||'block'),valid=gate==='playing'&&handsOn&&!played.includes(player),finished=gate==='done'&&phaseLength!==null&&records.length===total+1;
const reset=(fresh=false)=>{if(fresh){setDeck(shuffleDeck());setDsu(assignLeaders(players));}setRecords(initialHistory());setGate('start');setPhaseLength(null);setDuration(10);setLateWip(3);setWipChoice(3);setInspect(0);setDay(1);setTasks(freshBoard());setPlayer(1);setSelected(1);setPlayed([]);setBlackParts({});setDayEvents([]);setResetDialog(false);setDsuChecks([false,false,false]);setDsuNotes('');};
const startAuto=(reshuffle)=>{const d=reshuffle?shuffleDeck():deck,l=reshuffle?assignLeaders(players):dsu;if(reshuffle){setDeck(d);setDsu(l);}setRecords(runSpan(initialHistory(),1,20,players,d,l,3));setInspect(20);setGate('duration');setPhaseLength(null);setLateWip(3);};
const startManual=()=>{setRecords(initialHistory());setTasks(freshBoard());setDay(1);setPlayer(1);setSelected(1);setPlayed([]);setBlackParts({});setDayEvents([]);setDsuChecks([false,false,false]);setDsuNotes('');setGate('playing');};
const chooseDuration=()=>{setPhaseLength(duration);if(mode==='auto'){setRecords(runSpan(records,21,30,players,deck,dsu,3));setInspect(30);setGate(duration===10?'done':'wip');}else{setTasks(freshBoard());setDay(21);setPlayer(1);setSelected(1);setPlayed([]);setBlackParts({});setDayEvents([]);setDsuChecks([false,false,false]);setDsuNotes('');setGate(isFacilitated?'dsu':'playing');}};
const chooseLate=()=>{setLateWip(wipChoice);if(mode==='auto'){setRecords(runSpan(records,31,40,players,deck,dsu,wipChoice));setInspect(40);setGate('done');}else{setDay(31);setPlayer(1);setSelected(1);setPlayed([]);setBlackParts({});setDayEvents([]);setDsuChecks([false,false,false]);setDsuNotes('');setGate(isFacilitated?'dsu':'playing');}};
const allowedFor=(id,types)=>valid&&options.options.find(o=>o.id===id&&types.includes(o.type));
const dropTask=(status)=>{const id=draggedTask;setDraggedTask(null);setDragOverColumn(null);if(id===null||!valid)return;const item=tasks.find(t=>t.id===id);if(!item||status!==item.status+1)return;const move=allowedFor(id,item.status===0?['pull']:['advance','helpAdvance']);if(move)act(move.type,id);};
const handleDrop=(event,status)=>{event.preventDefault();const id=draggedTask??Number(event.dataTransfer.getData('text/plain'));if(!Number.isInteger(id)||id<=0)return;setDraggedTask(id);setDragOverColumn(null);const item=tasks.find(t=>t.id===id);if(!valid||!item||status!==item.status+1)return;const move=allowedFor(id,item.status===0?['pull']:['advance','helpAdvance']);if(move)act(move.type,id);setDraggedTask(null);};
const finishTurn=()=>{setPlayed(old=>[...old,player]);setPlayer(old=>people.find(p=>p>old&&!played.includes(p))||people.find(p=>p!==old&&!played.includes(p))||old);};
const act=(type,id)=>{if(!valid||!options.options.some(o=>o.type===type&&o.id===id))return;setTasks(old=>applyAction(old,player,day,type,id));setRecentAction({id,type,stamp:Date.now()});setDayEvents(old=>[...old,`P${player}: ${type} Task #${id}`]);if(type==='block'){setBlackParts(old=>({...old,[player]:'pull'}));}else finishTurn();};
const finishDay=()=>{if(played.length!==players)return;setRecords(old=>[...old,{day,tasks:tasks.map(t=>({...t})),events:day>10?[`P${dsu[day]} leads the Daily DSU`,...dayEvents]:[...dayEvents]}]);setInspect(day);setDayEvents([]);if(day===20){setGate('duration');return;}if(day===30){setGate(phaseLength===20?'wip':'done');return;}if(day===40){setGate('done');return;}setDay(old=>old+1);setPlayer(1);setSelected(1);setPlayed([]);setBlackParts({});setDsuChecks([false,false,false]);setDsuNotes('');if(isFacilitated&&day+1>10)setGate('dsu');};
const completeDsu=()=>{if(!isFacilitated||gate!=='dsu'||!dsuComplete)return;setDayEvents(e=>[...e,`DSU led by Player ${dsu[day]}: discussion completed${dsuNotes.trim()?` — ${dsuNotes.trim()}`:''}`]);setGate('playing');};
const activeWipLimit=currentDay<=10?null:currentDay<=30?3:lateWip;
const wipStatus=(status)=>{if(status!==1&&status!==2)return null;const used=board.filter(t=>t.status===status).length;if(activeWipLimit===null)return {used,limit:null,state:'unlimited',label:'No WIP limit'};return {used,limit:activeWipLimit,state:used>activeWipLimit?'exceeded':used===activeWipLimit?'full':'available',label:used>activeWipLimit?'WIP LIMIT EXCEEDED':used===activeWipLimit?'AT CAPACITY — FINISH BEFORE PULLING':'CAPACITY AVAILABLE'};};
const currentPolicy=activeWipLimit===null?'Unlimited':`${activeWipLimit} / ${activeWipLimit}`;
const eligibleActions=valid&&gate==='playing'?options.options:[];
const eligibleIds=new Set(eligibleActions.map(x=>x.id));
const taskHints=Array.from(new Set(eligibleActions.map(x=>x.type)));
const actionHint=!valid?'This player has already finished their turn.':playingCard.red?(taskHints.includes('pull')?'Select a highlighted task to pull, or choose an available own action.':taskHints.some(x=>x.startsWith('help'))?'Your own moves are unavailable. Highlighted tasks belong to teammates you can help.':'Select a highlighted task to advance or unblock.'):(options.part==='block'?'STEP 1 · Highlighted cards can be BLOCKED. Select one, then click “1. Block own”.':'STEP 2 · Highlighted To-Do cards can be PULLED. If pulling is full, highlighted teammates’ tasks can be helped.');
return <section id="simulator" className="wrap sim-shell"><div className="sim-head"><div><div className="eyebrow dark">THE SIMULATION</div><h2>Three-phase Kanban experiment</h2><p>{gate==='start'?'Ready to begin':`Day ${currentDay} · ${phaseLength===null?'Duration selected after Day 20':`${total} days total`}`}</p></div><button className="btn secondary" onClick={()=>setResetDialog(x=>!x)}><RotateCcw size={16}/> Reset</button></div>
<div className="phase-grid">{[{name:'Unlimited WIP',range:'Days 1–10'},{name:'WIP 3 + DSU',range:'Days 11–20'},{name:'Fresh board',range:phaseLength===null?'Starts Day 21':`Days 21–${total}`}].map((x,i)=><div key={i} className={'phase-tile '+(gate!=='start'&&phaseOf(Math.max(1,currentDay))===i+1?'active':'')}><b>Phase {i+1}</b><span>{x.name}</span><small>{x.range}</small></div>)}</div>
{resetDialog&&<div className="panel compact"><label className="radio-line"><input type="checkbox" checked={resetFresh} onChange={e=>setResetFresh(e.target.checked)}/> Reshuffle cards and DSU assignments</label><div className="button-row"><button className="btn primary" onClick={()=>reset(resetFresh)}>Confirm reset</button><button className="btn secondary" onClick={()=>setResetDialog(false)}>Cancel</button></div></div>}
{gate==='start'&&<div className="panel"><h3>Set up your workshop</h3><label className="form-label">Players</label><div className="button-row">{[3,4,5].map(v=><button key={v} className={'btn option '+(players===v?'selected':'')} onClick={()=>{setPlayers(v);setDeck(shuffleDeck());setDsu(assignLeaders(v));}}>{v} players</button>)}</div><div className="name-setup"><b>Player names <span className="muted small-text">(optional)</span></b><p className="muted small-text">Add the names of the participants. Blank names will continue to display as P1, P2, etc.</p><div className="name-grid">{people.map(p=><label className="name-field" key={p}><span>P{p}</span><input type="text" maxLength={30} placeholder={`Player ${p} name`} value={playerNames[p-1]||''} onChange={e=>setPlayerNames(old=>old.map((v,i)=>i===p-1?e.target.value:v))}/></label>)}</div></div><label className="form-label">Simulation mode</label><div className="button-row">{[['manual','Manual play'],['facilitated','Facilitated team'],['auto','Automatic']].map(([v,label])=><button key={v} className={'btn option '+(mode===v?'selected ':'')+(v==='auto'?'mode-automatic':'')} onClick={()=>setMode(v)}>{label}</button>)}</div><div className="button-row spaced">{mode==='auto'?<><button className="btn primary" onClick={()=>startAuto(true)}><Shuffle size={16}/> New simulation · Days 1–20</button><button className="btn secondary" onClick={()=>startAuto(false)}>Replay same cards</button></>:<button className="btn primary" onClick={startManual}><Play size={16}/> {isFacilitated?'Start facilitated session':'Start manual simulation'}</button>}</div>{isFacilitated&&<div className="facilitator-info"><b>One operator, {players} decision-makers.</b><p>Players announce their own moves in Phase 1 without a stand-up. Starting on Day 11, a random player leads a mandatory DSU before the cards are revealed. The operator clicks each legal move.</p><div className="walkthrough"><strong>Daily facilitation walkthrough</strong><ol><li><b>Days 1–10:</b> No DSU. Each player makes an individual choice; the operator records it.</li><li><b>From Day 11:</b> The simulator pauses on a DSU screen before showing the playing cards.</li><li><b>DSU leader:</b> Ask what was completed, what matters today, and where blockers need help. Tick each prompt after discussing it.</li><li><b>Reveal cards:</b> Click “Complete DSU · Reveal cards.” Select each player's card; glowing task notes show their legal choices.</li><li><b>Next day:</b> Finish everyone's turns, then advance to the next DSU checkpoint.</li></ol></div></div>}<p className="muted small-text">Each visitor uses an independent browser simulation. The 52-card deck is shuffled without replacement and the same 10-day sequence is replayed across phases.</p><p className="muted small-text">Card rules adapted from <a href="https://www.agendashift.com/resources/featureban" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Featureban by Mike Burrows</a> under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CC BY-SA 4.0</a>. This digital adaptation adds facilitation and flow-measurement features. <a href="#about-me">Full acknowledgment</a>.</p></div>}
{gate==='duration'&&<div className="decision panel"><div className="eyebrow dark">AFTER DAY 20 · DECISION 1</div><h3>Choose Phase 3's duration</h3><p>Start fresh with 30 backlog tasks and WIP 3 in Working on and Review.</p>{[10,20].map(v=><label className="radio-line" key={v}><input type="radio" name="duration" checked={duration===v} onChange={()=>setDuration(v)}/>{v} days — {v===10?'finish on Day 30':'continue to Day 40 with a WIP experiment at Day 31'}</label>)}<button className="btn primary spaced" onClick={chooseDuration}>Start Phase 3 <ArrowRight size={16}/></button></div>}
{gate==='dsu'&&isFacilitated&&<div className="decision panel dsu-checkpoint"><div className="eyebrow dark">DAY {day} · TEAM CHECKPOINT</div><h3>Daily DSU — led by {playerLabel(dsu[day])}</h3><p>Before the operator reveals the day's cards, ask the group to listen, coordinate, and identify where help is needed. The DSU cannot be skipped in Facilitated Team Mode.</p>{['What did we finish or learn yesterday?','What should we focus on today?','Which blockers need help, and from whom?'].map((prompt,i)=><label className="dsu-check" key={i}><input type="checkbox" checked={dsuChecks[i]} onChange={e=>setDsuChecks(old=>old.map((v,j)=>j===i?e.target.checked:v))}/><span>{prompt}</span></label>)}<label className="form-label" htmlFor="dsu-notes">Operator notes (optional)</label><textarea id="dsu-notes" className="dsu-notes" rows={2} value={dsuNotes} onChange={e=>setDsuNotes(e.target.value)} placeholder="One thing the team agreed to do differently today…"/><button className="btn primary spaced" disabled={!dsuComplete} onClick={completeDsu}>Complete DSU · Reveal cards <ArrowRight size={16}/></button><p className="chart-note">The DSU records a real discussion; it does not automatically move cards or guarantee a better result.</p></div>}
{gate==='wip'&&<div className="decision panel"><div className="eyebrow dark">START OF DAY 31 · DECISION 2</div><h3>Experiment with WIP limits</h3><p>Day 30 is complete. The board, blockers, and task ages carry forward. Choose the limit for both Working on and Review for Days 31–40. WIP 2 is available for any team size: fewer parallel tasks may encourage finishing and helping, but can also increase waiting when work is blocked. Discuss your prediction before selecting.</p>{[2,3,4,...(players===5?[5]:[])].map(v=><label className="radio-line" key={v}><input type="radio" name="latewip" checked={wipChoice===v} onChange={()=>setWipChoice(v)}/> WIP {v}{v===3?' — keep the existing limit':v===2?' — reduce parallel work':''}</label>)}<button className="btn primary spaced" onClick={chooseLate}>Apply WIP {wipChoice} and begin Day 31 <ArrowRight size={16}/></button></div>}
{gate!=='start'&&<>{mode==='auto'&&records.length>1&&<div className="panel compact"><div className="section-row"><b>Inspect Day {inspect}</b><span className="muted small-text">Simulated through Day {records[records.length-1].day}</span></div><input className="range" type="range" min="1" max={records[records.length-1].day} value={inspect} onChange={e=>setInspect(Number(e.target.value))}/></div>}
<div className="panel">{gate==='dsu'&&isFacilitated?<div className="facilitator-info"><b>Cards are hidden until the DSU is completed.</b><p>The board remains visible. Ask everyone to listen before reacting to a new draw.</p></div>:<><div className="section-row"><h3>Daily playing cards</h3><span className="muted small-text">Standard 52-card deck</span></div>{currentDay>10?<div className="dsu"><Users size={18}/><div><span>Today's randomly selected DSU leader</span><b>{playerLabel(dsu[currentDay])}</b><small>Review finished work, current goals, and blockers.</small></div></div>:<p className="muted small-text">Phase 1 · No assigned Daily Stand-Up leader</p>}<div className="cards-grid" style={{gridTemplateColumns:`repeat(${players},minmax(0,1fr))`}}>{people.map(p=>{const c=drawCard(deck,Math.max(1,currentDay),players,p);return <button key={p} className={classCard(c)+(handsOn&&player===p&&gate==='playing'?' picked':'')+(handsOn&&played.includes(p)?' finished-card':'')} onClick={()=>{if(handsOn&&gate==='playing')setPlayer(p)}}><small className="card-player-label">{playerLabel(p)}</small><b>{c.rank}{c.suit}</b><span>{c.red?'RED':'BLACK'}</span>{handsOn&&played.includes(p)?<small>✓ Done</small>:handsOn&&player===p&&gate==='playing'?<small>● CURRENT</small>:null}</button>})}</div>{handsOn&&gate==='playing'&&<div className="turn-info"><b>{playerLabel(player)} · {playingCard.red?'Red':'Black'} card</b><p>{playingCard.red?'Advance, unblock, or pull one task. Help another player only when none of those actions is possible.':options.part==='block'?'Step 1: Block your own task, then attempt to pull.':'Step 2: Pull new work. If pulling is impossible, help another player.'}</p>{isFacilitated&&<small>Operator: ask {playerLabel(player)} for a decision; only highlighted tasks are currently legal.</small>}</div>}</>}</div>
{handsOn&&gate==='playing'&&<div className={'day-advance-bar '+(played.length===players?'ready':'waiting')} role="region" aria-label="Advance simulation day"><div className="day-advance-status"><strong>Day {day} · {played.length}/{players} players finished</strong><span>{played.length===players?'All players have finished. Ready for the next day.':'Complete every player’s card action to continue.'}</span></div><button type="button" className="btn primary day-advance-button" disabled={played.length!==players} onClick={finishDay}>{day===20?'Complete Phase 2':day===30?'Complete Day 30':day===40?'Finish simulation':'Next day'} <ArrowRight size={16}/></button></div>}
<div className="section-row board-heading"><h3>Kanban board</h3><span className="muted small-text">WIP: {currentPolicy}</span></div>
{handsOn&&gate==='playing'&&<div className="eligibility-banner"><div><b>{playerLabel(player)} · {playingCard.red?'Red card':`Black card — ${options.part==='block'?'Block step':'Pull/help step'}`}</b><p>Drag a highlighted ticket one column to the right, or use the buttons directly on that ticket. Add or remove blockers on the ticket. All card rules and WIP limits still apply.</p></div><span className="eligible-count">{eligibleIds.size} eligible {eligibleIds.size===1?'task':'tasks'}</span></div>}
<div className="board-scroll"><div className="kanban-board">{COLUMNS.map((name,status)=><div key={name}
  className={'column '+(wipStatus(status)?'wip-'+wipStatus(status).state:'')+(dragOverColumn===status?' task-drop-target':'')}
  onDragOver={event=>{if(!handsOn||gate!=='playing'||draggedTask===null)return;const item=tasks.find(t=>t.id===draggedTask);if(item&&status===item.status+1&&allowedFor(draggedTask,item.status===0?['pull']:['advance','helpAdvance'])){event.preventDefault();event.dataTransfer.dropEffect='move';setDragOverColumn(status);}}}
  onDragLeave={event=>{if(!event.currentTarget.contains(event.relatedTarget))setDragOverColumn(null);}}
  onDrop={event=>handleDrop(event,status)}>
  <div className="column-heading"><b>{name}</b><span>{board.filter(t=>t.status===status).length}</span></div>
  {[1,2].includes(status)&&<div className="wip-indicator" role="status" aria-label={`${name}: ${wipStatus(status).used} tasks; ${wipStatus(status).label}`}><small className="wip-label">WIP {wipStatus(status).used} / {wipStatus(status).limit===null?'∞':wipStatus(status).limit}</small>{wipStatus(status).limit!==null&&<><div className="wip-meter" aria-hidden="true"><div className="wip-meter-fill" style={{width:`${Math.min(100,100*wipStatus(status).used/wipStatus(status).limit)}%`}}/></div><strong className="wip-state-label">{wipStatus(status).state==='exceeded'?'⚠ ':wipStatus(status).state==='full'?'● ':'✓ '}{wipStatus(status).label}</strong></>}</div>}
  <div className="task-list">{board.filter(t=>t.status===status).map(t=>{
   const move=allowedFor(t.id,status===0?['pull']:['advance','helpAdvance']);
   const blocker=allowedFor(t.id,t.blocked?['unblock','helpUnblock']:['block']);
   const canUse=handsOn&&gate==='playing';
   return <div key={t.id} draggable={Boolean(canUse&&move)}
    onDragStart={event=>{if(!move){event.preventDefault();return;}setDraggedTask(t.id);event.dataTransfer.effectAllowed='move';event.dataTransfer.setData('text/plain',String(t.id));}}
    onDragEnd={()=>{setDraggedTask(null);setDragOverColumn(null);}}
    className={'sticky task-interactive '+(canUse&&eligibleIds.has(t.id)?'eligible ':'')+(canUse&&selected===t.id?'chosen ':'')+(canUse&&!eligibleIds.has(t.id)?'unavailable ':'')+(move?'task-draggable ':'')+(recentAction?.id===t.id?'task-just-changed '+(recentAction.type.toLowerCase().includes('block')?'task-block-flash':'task-move-flash'):'')}
    onClick={()=>{if(canUse)setSelected(t.id)}}>
    <div className="task-title"><b>Task #{t.id}</b>{move&&<span className="task-drag-grip" title="Drag to next column">⠿</span>}</div>
    {t.owner&&<small>Owner {playerLabel(t.owner)}</small>}
    {t.started!==null&&<small>◷ {age(t,currentDay)}d</small>}
    {t.blocked&&<strong className="task-blocked-badge">● BLOCKED</strong>}
    {canUse&&<div className="task-inline-actions">
      {move&&<button type="button" className="task-inline-btn task-move-btn" onClick={event=>{event.stopPropagation();act(move.type,t.id)}}>{status===0?'Pull →':status===1?'To Review →':'To Done →'}</button>}
      {blocker&&<button type="button" className={'task-inline-btn '+(t.blocked?'task-unblock-btn':'task-block-btn')} onClick={event=>{event.stopPropagation();act(blocker.type,t.id)}}>{t.blocked?'Remove blocker':'Add blocker'}</button>}
    </div>}
   </div>})}</div></div>)}</div></div>
{handsOn&&gate==='playing'&&<div className="panel compact"><div className="section-row"><div><b>{played.length}/{players} turns finished</b><p className="muted small-text">Use the actions on the tickets above. The next day remains locked until all players have finished.</p></div><button className="btn secondary small" disabled={!valid||!options.canPass} onClick={()=>{setDayEvents(e=>[...e,`P${player}: No legal move`]);finishTurn();}}>No legal move</button></div>
<details className="task-fallback-actions"><summary>Alternative controls (accessibility)</summary><div className="section-row"><h3>{playerLabel(player)} — action</h3><span className="muted small-text">Selected Task #{selected}</span></div><div className="action-grid">{(playingCard.red?[['advance','Advance own'],['unblock','Unblock own'],['pull','Pull new'],['helpAdvance','Help advance'],['helpUnblock','Help unblock']]:[['block','1. Block own'],['pull','2. Pull new'],['helpAdvance','Help advance'],['helpUnblock','Help unblock']]).map(([key,label])=><button key={key} className="btn secondary" disabled={!valid||!options.options.some(o=>o.type===key&&o.id===selected)} onClick={()=>act(key,selected)}>{label}</button>)}</div></details>
</div>}
<div className="panel"><h3>Live metrics</h3><div className="metrics-grid"><Stat label="Backlog" value={live.backlog}/><Stat label="In Progress" value={live.inProgress}/><Stat label="Blocked" value={live.blocked}/><Stat label="Completed" value={live.completed}/></div></div>
{mode==='auto'&&records.length>1&&<details className="panel log"><summary>Day {inspect} action log</summary>{(records.find(r=>r.day===inspect)?.events||[]).map((event,i)=><p key={i}>{renameLog(event)}</p>)}</details>}
</>}
{finished&&<Results key={`${phaseLength}-${lateWip}-${records.length}`} history={records} total={total} phaseLength={phaseLength} lateWip={lateWip} playerNames={playerNames} players={players}/>}</section>}
function Footer(){return <footer className="footer"><div className="wrap">Kanban Flow Lab · An interactive learning exercise. Outcomes illustrate simulated choices and are not proof of causal effects.</div></footer>}
function HowDetails(){return <section className="wrap how-content" id="how-details"><div className="eyebrow dark">FACILITATED &amp; COLLABORATIVE SIMULATIONS</div><h2>How the foundational simulation works</h2><p className="how-lede">Experience how the way we manage work affects what gets finished. You’ll work through three phases: first without limits on work in progress, then with limits, and finally by experimenting with different approaches. Compare the results to discover what helps work flow more effectively.</p><div className="how-phase-grid"><article className="how-card"><span className="how-step">01</span><h3>Phase 1 · Experience the Challenge</h3><p className="how-meta">Days 1–10 · Unlimited WIP</p><p>Start work without limits. Notice what happens when people keep starting tasks instead of focusing on finishing them.</p></article><article className="how-card"><span className="how-step">02</span><h3>Phase 2 · Introduce Focus</h3><p className="how-meta">Days 11–20 · WIP limit of 3</p><p>Limit work in progress and communicate daily. See how teamwork and finishing existing work change the results.</p></article><article className="how-card"><span className="how-step">03</span><h3>Phase 3 · Experiment and Learn</h3><p className="how-meta">Days 21–30, or through Day 40</p><p>Begin with a fresh board and WIP 3. Choose whether to continue for another ten days and try a different WIP limit. Compare what helps the team finish.</p></article></div><p className="how-lede" style={{marginBottom:24}}><strong>Looking for a different challenge?</strong> Flow Evolution Lab is the advanced experience: teams choose their own WIP limits, face changing demand and daily scenarios, and reflect on the consequences of their decisions.</p><div className="how-section-grid"><section className="how-panel"><BookOpen size={25}/><h2>The cards introduce variation</h2><p>Players draw from a shuffled 52-card deck. Red and black cards determine available actions under the game rules. The variation helps participants see that results are not always predictable—and encourages them to question how their policies respond.</p><p>Replay the same card sequence across the first two phases to make the comparison more meaningful.</p></section><section className="how-panel"><Users size={25}/><h2>Three ways to explore flow</h2><p><strong>Facilitated:</strong> One person runs the simulation on a shared screen while three to five players discuss decisions. It also supports manual and automatic practice.</p><p><strong>Collaborative:</strong> Players participate from their own devices using a shared simulation room.</p><p><strong>Flow Evolution Lab:</strong> Experienced teams handle changing demand, make policy decisions, and reflect on consequences.</p></section><section className="how-panel"><ChartColumnIncreasing size={25}/><h2>Measure the system</h2><p>Explore cumulative flow, throughput, lead time, observed 75th, 85th, and 95th percentiles, and the aging of unfinished work.</p><p>Use the metrics to ask better questions—not to judge individual players.</p></section><section className="how-panel"><Info size={25}/><h2>Reflect and learn</h2><p>At the end of each phase, compare how much work was started versus completed, discuss blockers, and consider how limiting WIP changed teamwork and predictability.</p><p>Facilitated simulations run in the current browser page; results are not saved between visits.</p></section></div></section>}

function FacilitatedHero(){return <section className="facilitated-hero"><div className="wrap"><a href="#home" className="back-link back-link-light"><ArrowLeft size={16}/> All simulation experiences</a><div className="eyebrow">FACILITATED SIMULATION</div><h1>One screen.<br/><em>Shared decisions.</em></h1><p>Lead a guided Kanban experiment with your class or team. Explore flow, WIP limits, blockers, and teamwork together in real time.</p></div></section>}
function AboutMe(){return <div className="about-page" id="about-me"><section className="about-hero"><div className="wrap about-hero-layout"><div className="about-hero-copy"><div className="eyebrow">ABOUT THE CREATOR</div><h1>Brent Greenfield</h1><p className="about-tagline">Transformation &amp; Delivery Leader · Agile &amp; Kanban Coach · Workshop Facilitator</p><p className="about-intro">Helping people and organizations see how work really happens, improve collaboration, and deliver better outcomes.</p><div className="about-hero-actions" style={{display:"flex",alignItems:"center",flexWrap:"wrap",gap:"12px"}}><a className="hero-link" href="mailto:greenfieldbrent@gmail.com"><Mail size={17}/> Get in touch</a><a className="hero-link about-linkedin-hero" style={{background:"#173650",color:"#ffffff"}} href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/brentgreenfield" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="View LinkedIn profile"><Linkedin size={17}/> LinkedIn profile <ExternalLink size={14}/></a></div></div><div className="about-portrait-frame"><img src="/images/brent-greenfield.jpg" alt="Professional portrait of Brent Greenfield" loading="eager" width="900" height="1125" /></div></div></section><section className="wrap about-content"><div className="about-main"><div className="eyebrow dark">MY BACKGROUND</div><h2>Transformation starts with understanding the system.</h2><p>I bring nearly two decades of experience in banking, project delivery, and organizational change. My work spans project management, Agile coaching, Kanban systems, team development, and the practical use of data to understand and improve how work flows.</p><p>As a Kanban and Agile coach, I help teams make their work visible, uncover obstacles, establish useful feedback loops, and move from starting more work to finishing what matters. My focus is not simply adopting a framework. It is helping people understand why they work the way they do and how to improve together.</p><p>I created <strong>Kanban Flow Lab</strong> as a hands-on learning experience. Rather than just hearing about WIP limits, blockers, collaboration, and flow metrics, participants can see and experience their effects—and discuss what the data does and does not tell them.</p><section aria-label="Origins and acknowledgments" style={{marginTop:'1.6rem',marginBottom:'1.6rem'}}><h2>Origins &amp; Acknowledgments</h2><p>Kanban Flow Lab is an independently developed digital teaching tool that adapts card-based simulation rules from <a href="https://www.agendashift.com/resources/featureban" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Featureban</a>, created by Mike Burrows of Agendashift. The experience adds interactive gameplay, facilitator-led activities, and flow measurements to support reflection and discovery.</p><p>The Featureban-derived material and adaptations are shared under the <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International license (CC BY-SA 4.0)</a>. Changes include digital interactions, structured phases, and additional measurement and facilitation features. Kanban Flow Lab is not affiliated with or endorsed by Agendashift.</p></section><blockquote>“Data should tell the story of the system—not become a scorecard for judging people.”</blockquote><h2>How I approach change</h2><p>Meaningful change happens when leaders make it safe to learn. I combine practical experiments, visual management, and measures of flow with an emphasis on listening, shared ownership, and continuous improvement.</p><p>I'm especially interested in how teams can use Kanban, change management, and thoughtful technology adoption to improve results without losing the human side of work.</p></div><aside className="about-side"><div className="about-info-card"><Award size={23}/><h3>Professional qualifications</h3><ul><li>Kanban Coaching Professional (KCP)</li><li>SAFe Practice Consultant (SPC)</li><li>Advanced Certified ScrumMaster (A-CSM)</li><li>Lean Six Sigma Black Belt</li><li>Project management and Scrum Master experience</li></ul></div><div className="about-info-card"><GraduationCap size={23}/><h3>Continuing education</h3><p>Professional MBA student at Florida International University, extending a career-long commitment to leadership and business learning.</p></div><div className="about-info-card"><Compass size={23}/><h3>Speaking &amp; workshops</h3><p>Interactive sessions on flow, leadership, teamwork, and measuring improvement—built around learning by doing.</p></div><div className="about-contact" id="contact"><h3>Let's connect</h3><p>Interested in a workshop, a speaking session, or a conversation about improving how work gets done?</p><a className="about-email" href="mailto:greenfieldbrent@gmail.com"><Mail size={18}/> greenfieldbrent@gmail.com</a><a className="about-email" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/brentgreenfield" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><Linkedin size={18}/> linkedin.com/in/brentgreenfield <ExternalLink size={13}/></a><a className="btn secondary" href="#facilitated"><ArrowLeft size={16}/> Explore the simulation</a></div></aside></section></div>}

function JourneyPage(){
 const [enlargedImage,setEnlargedImage]=useState(null);
 const [journeyMilestone,setJourneyMilestone]=useState(0);
 const firstThirtyDays=[
  {day:'Day 0',date:'Sep 9, 2024',label:'Observe',title:'Start observing',detail:'Data collection begins. The first goal is to understand how work moves before trying to change the system.',question:'Where is work waiting, and what do we know about our starting point?'},
  {day:'Day 7',date:'Sep 18, 2024',label:'Learn',title:'Build shared understanding',detail:'Kanban training gives the team a common language to discuss workflow, work in progress, and how work gets finished.',question:'Which existing practices help us, and which policies are worth examining?'},
  {day:'Day 10',date:'Sep 23, 2024',label:'Experiment',title:'Introduce WIP limits',detail:'The team introduces WIP limits as a practical experiment. The dashboard remains a way to observe how the system responds.',question:'What changes in waiting, completion, and collaboration after limiting simultaneous work?'}
 ];
 const chapters=[
  {n:'01',tag:'SEE THE WORK',heading:'Making the invisible visible',image:'/images/journey/early-dashboard.webp',alt:'Historical Excel dashboard with cumulative flow and lead time charts',body:'The first dashboard was intentionally simple. Alongside the measures, I recorded when collection began, when the team learned the practices, and when we introduced WIP limits.',lesson:'A useful improvement story includes the changes made to the system, not just the latest numbers.'},
  {n:'02',tag:'ASK BETTER QUESTIONS',heading:'Understanding what the averages hide',image:'/images/journey/expanded-metrics.webp',alt:'Historical dashboard with expanded flow measures',body:'As questions changed, the dashboard changed too. Lead-time distributions, cumulative flow, and other perspectives helped us investigate how work moved and where it waited.',lesson:'One metric can raise a question. Several perspectives can help a team explore it.'},
  {n:'03',tag:'CONNECT TO DECISIONS',heading:'Looking at aging work and different demand',image:'/images/journey/flow-and-aging.webp',alt:'Historical dashboard showing aging and flow charts',body:'The next step was to make aging work and accumulating demand easier to discuss. Capacity views helped connect the flow conversation to what teams chose to start and finish.',lesson:'Visibility matters when it changes what we decide to do next.'},
  {n:'04',tag:'DIFFERENT TEAMS · SHARED PRINCIPLES',heading:'Different teams. Shared principles. Continuous improvement.',image:'/images/journey/power-bi-flow.webp',alt:'Power BI flow metrics dashboard with cumulative flow, throughput, lead time and organizational filters',body:'As the dashboard expanded from team to organizational views, I saw the same opportunities across Kanban teams, Scrum teams, and traditional project teams. Each had different ways of working, but all could benefit from seeing where work waited, what was getting finished, and where quality or delivery was at risk.',lesson:'A framework can provide helpful practices. The improvement begins when a team understands its own work and chooses what problem to solve next.'},
  {n:'05',tag:'FORECAST WITH UNCERTAINTY',heading:'From reporting the past to forecasting the future',image:'/images/journey/monte-carlo-forecast.webp',alt:'Power BI Monte Carlo forecasting view with historical throughput, simulated delivery distribution, percentile outcomes and calendar ranges',body:'The next step was using historical throughput as a basis for Monte Carlo simulations. Rather than treating a single target date as certain, I could examine a range of possible outcomes and discuss the confidence behind delivery plans.',lesson:'Forecasts are ranges informed by historical evidence, not promises. They make uncertainty visible so teams can make better choices.'}
 ];
 return <div className="journey-page">
  <section className="journey-hero"><div className="wrap"><div className="eyebrow">BEHIND KANBAN FLOW LAB</div><h1>The Journey: <em>From Visibility to Understanding</em></h1><p>My first metrics dashboard was an Excel workbook. It did not begin with every metric or a perfect design. It began with a question: what can we learn about how our work moves?</p><a className="journey-scroll" href="#journey-chapters" onClick={e=>{e.preventDefault();document.getElementById('journey-chapters')?.scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth'})}}>Explore the journey ↓</a></div></section>
  <section className="wrap journey-intro"><p><strong>The point was never to build the biggest dashboard.</strong> It was to create visibility, learn from change, and make it easier for people to improve together.</p><div className="journey-note">These examples document how the dashboards evolved. Selected identifying labels in the shared screenshots have been obscured. The stories describe learning and decisions, not proof that any one change caused a particular result.</div></section>
  <section id="journey-chapters" className="wrap journey-chapters" aria-label="The journey chapters">{chapters.map(ch=><React.Fragment key={ch.n}><article className="journey-chapter"><div className="journey-chapter-copy"><span className="journey-overline">{ch.n} · {ch.tag}</span><h2>{ch.heading}</h2><p>{ch.body}</p><p className="journey-lesson"><strong>What I learned:</strong> {ch.lesson}</p></div><div className={"journey-visual"+(Number(ch.n)>=4?" journey-visual--powerbi":"")}>{ch.image?<>{ch.n==='04'?<button className="journey-image-zoom" type="button" onClick={()=>setEnlargedImage({src:ch.image,alt:ch.alt})} aria-label="Enlarge Power BI metrics dashboard"><img src={ch.image} alt={ch.alt} loading="lazy"/><span className="journey-zoom-label">Click to enlarge ↗</span></button>:<img src={ch.image} alt={ch.alt} loading="lazy"/>}<span className="journey-archive-tag">Dashboard evolution · selected labels hidden</span></>:<div className="journey-modern"><ChartColumnIncreasing size={56}/><b>Power BI</b><span>The tools became more capable.<br/>The learning remains the focus.</span></div>}</div></article>{ch.n==='04'&&<section className="journey-scrum-story" aria-labelledby="journey-scrum-heading">
   <div className="journey-scrum-copy"><span className="journey-overline">A CLOSER LOOK · SCRUM AND FLOW</span><h3 id="journey-scrum-heading">The work matters more than the ritual.</h3>
   <p>Scrum Master training gave me useful ways to think about events, story quality, estimating, and collaboration. But training can sometimes describe the practices of a well-established team before people have had the chance to learn together. Teams grow by experiencing the work, discussing what happens, and improving a step at a time.</p>
   <p>I often heard, “We need better stories.” Sometimes that is true. Better descriptions can improve shared understanding, and estimation can prompt valuable conversations. But before adding another practice, I wanted to ask: <strong>What problem are we actually trying to solve?</strong></p>
   <p>On this Scrum team's dashboard, sprint velocity, commitment reliability, and carryover sit alongside WIP, blockers, throughput, aging work, lead time, and a cumulative flow diagram. They offer different views of the same delivery system. No one number determines whether the team is doing well, and the purpose is not to rank people.</p>
   <p className="journey-lesson"><strong>What I learned:</strong> Start with the team as it is. Use evidence and conversations to select practices that help it deliver valuable, quality work more effectively and sustainably—not because a practice is fashionable or prescribed.</p></div>
   <figure className="journey-scrum-figure"><button type="button" className="journey-image-zoom" onClick={()=>setEnlargedImage({src:'/images/journey/scrum-team-flow.webp',alt:'Original anonymized Scrum team Power BI dashboard showing both sprint measures and system flow metrics'})} aria-label="Enlarge Scrum team Power BI metrics dashboard"><img src="/images/journey/scrum-team-flow.webp" alt="Anonymized Scrum team Power BI dashboard with sprint velocity, commitment reliability, cumulative flow, WIP aging, throughput and lead time" loading="lazy"/><span className="journey-zoom-label">Click to enlarge ↗</span></button><figcaption>Scrum team example · sprint measures and flow measures viewed together. Select the image to inspect it.</figcaption></figure>
  </section>}{ch.n==='01'&&<section className="journey-early-experiment" aria-label="Interactive history of the first thirty days">
   <div className="journey-early-header"><div><span className="journey-overline">A CLOSER LOOK · THE ORIGINAL 2024 WORKBOOK</span><h3>The first 30 days of learning</h3><p>The first workbook tracked daily snapshots as well as the moments when the team changed its practices. Select a milestone to follow the story.</p></div><span className="journey-early-count">3 documented milestones</span></div>
   <div className="journey-early-steps" role="group" aria-label="Choose a recorded milestone">{firstThirtyDays.map((m,i)=><button key={m.day} type="button" className={'journey-early-step'+(journeyMilestone===i?' is-active':'')} aria-pressed={journeyMilestone===i} onClick={()=>setJourneyMilestone(i)}><span className="journey-early-day">{m.day}</span><strong>{m.label}</strong><span className="journey-early-date">{m.date}</span></button>)}</div>
   <div className="journey-early-detail" aria-live="polite"><div><span className="journey-early-selected">{firstThirtyDays[journeyMilestone].day} · {firstThirtyDays[journeyMilestone].date}</span><h4>{firstThirtyDays[journeyMilestone].title}</h4><p>{firstThirtyDays[journeyMilestone].detail}</p></div><div className="journey-early-question"><strong>Question to explore</strong><p>{firstThirtyDays[journeyMilestone].question}</p></div></div>
   <p className="journey-early-caveat">The workbook recorded these milestones; it does not establish that one practice alone caused later results. Changes in demand, work, and context matter too.</p>
  </section>}</React.Fragment>)}</section>
  {enlargedImage&&<div className="journey-image-overlay" role="presentation" onMouseDown={e=>{if(e.target===e.currentTarget)setEnlargedImage(null)}}><div className="journey-image-dialog" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-label="Enlarged Power BI dashboard"><button type="button" className="journey-image-close" aria-label="Close enlarged dashboard" onClick={()=>setEnlargedImage(null)}>Close ×</button><img src={enlargedImage.src} alt={enlargedImage.alt}/></div></div>}
  <section className="journey-timeline"><div className="wrap"><div className="eyebrow">THE PART I STILL VALUE MOST</div><h2>Record the changes, not just the results.</h2><p>On my earliest board, I recorded three moments alongside the metrics.</p><div className="journey-milestones"><div><b>Observe</b><span>Data collection begins</span></div><div><b>Learn</b><span>Team learns the Kanban practices</span></div><div><b>Experiment</b><span>WIP limits are introduced</span></div></div><p className="journey-caveat">Seeing flow change afterward gives us a question to investigate—not proof of cause and effect. Other changes in work, demand, and context also matter.</p></div></section>
  <section className="wrap journey-end"><span className="journey-overline">THE NEXT CHAPTER IS ALWAYS OPEN</span><h2>The story is still being written.</h2><p>My first Excel dashboard was not the finish line. Neither was Power BI or forecasting. Each improvement revealed another question—and another opportunity to learn.</p><p>Scrum, Kanban, and project management offer useful starting practices, but none can anticipate every challenge a team will face. When we look at the work together rather than pointing fingers or checking whether every recommended practice is in place, we can choose the improvement that matters now.</p><p className="journey-last-line">Make work visible. Learn from experience. Improve together. <strong>To be continued.</strong></p><div className="journey-actions"><a className="btn" href="#choose-simulation">Experience a simulation →</a><a href="#data-and-story">Understand the data →</a><a href="#flow-assessment">Explore an improvement →</a></div></section>
  <footer className="footer"><div className="wrap">Kanban Flow Lab · Leadership through experimentation.</div></footer>
 </div>;
}

function App(){
  const route=()=>{const hash=window.location.hash;
    return (hash==='#kmm-assessment'||hash==='#flow-assessment')?'assessment':
      hash==='#flow-evolution'?'evolution':
      hash==='#journey'?'journey':
      (hash==='#data-and-story'||hash.startsWith('#metric-'))?'story':
      hash==='#about-me'||hash==='#contact'?'about':
      hash==='#how-it-works'?'home':hash==='#facilitated'||hash==='#simulator'?'facilitated':'home';
  };
  const [page,setPage]=useState(route);
  useEffect(()=>{
    const update=()=>setPage(route());
    window.addEventListener('hashchange',update);
    return ()=>window.removeEventListener('hashchange',update);
  },[]);
  useEffect(()=>{
    if(window.location.hash==='#choose-simulation'){
      document.getElementById(window.location.hash.slice(1))?.scrollIntoView();
    } else {
      window.scrollTo(0,0);
    }
  },[page]);
  return <><Nav page={page}/><main>
    {page==='journey'?<JourneyPage/>:page==='story'?<DataStory/>:page==='evolution'?<FlowEvolution/>:page==='assessment'?<FlowAssessment/>:page==='about'?<AboutMe/>:page==='facilitated'?
      <><FacilitatedHero/><Simulator/><Footer/></>:
      <><Intro/><LearningJourney/><ChooseSimulation/><WhyFlowWorks/><VideoPreviewPlaceholder/><div className="wrap journey-home-teaser"><div><span className="journey-overline">BEHIND THE LAB</span><h2>Every improvement starts somewhere.</h2><p>See how a simple Excel dashboard became a way to learn from teams, experiment with WIP limits, and ask better questions about flow.</p></div><a href="#journey">See the journey →</a></div><FoundationalDetails/><div className="wrap home-credit"><p>Simulation card rules adapted from <a href="https://www.agendashift.com/resources/featureban" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Featureban by Mike Burrows</a> under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CC BY-SA 4.0</a>. <a href="#about-me">Origins &amp; Acknowledgments</a>.</p></div><footer className="footer"><div className="wrap">Kanban Flow Lab · Leadership through experimentation.</div></footer></>}
  </main></>;
};
createRoot(document.getElementById('root')).render(<App/>);
